(1330, 'Aestora  Acne Spot Removal Serum', '1', 0, 35, 67, '1330', '1330', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Target blemishes, fade spots, and restore clarity — with smart actives in a lightweight formula.\nThis serum is designed for skin that’s acne‑prone or marked by past breakouts and spots. It works to:\nHelp calm and reduce active acne and visible blemishes.\nFade dark spots, post‑inflammatory hyperpigmentation and residual red marks.\nPromote smoother texture and more even skin tone.\nProvide a non‑greasy, fast‑absorbing finish so your skin feels comfortable and clean.\nSpot‑focused clarity — the targeted actives help address the “dew rise” of each blemish and its after‑mark.\nCorrects tone — by gently fading spots and balancing the appearance of skin.\nLightweight & oil‑friendly — designed so it doesn’t leave heavy residue, ideal for oily or combination skin types.\nDaily use ready — can be incorporated into morning and/or evening routines.\nThose experiencing frequent breakouts or recurring spots.\nPeople with visible dark marks, red or brown blemish scars who want a corrective serum.\nSkin types that prefer lighter textures rather than heavy creams.\nUsers who already have a basic regimen but want added spot‑correction and texture refinement.\nAqua, Butylene Glycol, Propanediol – foundational hydrating glycols for smoother application and quick absorption.\nAloe Vera Leaf Juice – offers soothing support to calm skin that has been irritated by breakout‑cycles.\nGlycerin – a humectant that draws moisture in, helping keep skin comfortable even while actives are working.\nSweet Almond Oil & Jojoba Oil – emollient lipids that help maintain skin barrier support and add a pleasant texture (especially helpful after acne flares leave dryness).\nCetearyl Alcohol / Ceteareth‑20 / Cetearyl Olivate / Sorbitan Olivate – gentle emulsifiers and stabilisers that hold the formula together while offering skin‑friendly feel.\nActive ingredients (based on your list) – though full actives aren’t specified, the inclusion of a mixture of humectants + soothing botanical oils suggests a balanced approach between treatment and comfort.\nAfter cleansing and toning your face, and before heavier creams, apply 2‑3 drops of the serum over the entire face (or concentrate on problem zones).\nGently pat to help absorption.\nFollow with your usual moisturiser or sunscreen (if used in the morning).\nFor best results: use consistently morning and/or night. Always include sun‑protection in your morning routine — actives may increase sun sensitivity.', 1485.00, NULL, 0, '[]', '[]', '[]', NULL, 0, 1, 1, '0', 0, 0, 0, 100, 'Pack', 0.00, 1, NULL, 165.00, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'flat_rate', 0.00, 0, NULL, 0, 'Aestora  Acne Spot Removal SerumPrice in BD', 'Aestora  Acne Spot Removal Serum Price in Bangladesh', NULL, NULL, 'aestora-acne-spot-removal-serum', 0.00, 0, 0.00, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Buy Now', 0, '2026-02-11 13:41:25', '2026-02-11 13:41:25'),
(1331, 'KLM Laboratories Glycolic Acid Cream 12% W/W GA - 12', '1', 0, 35, 320, '1331', '1331', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Ga-12 12%W/W Cream is used to treat skin problems like acne (pimples), acne scars, melasma, hyperpigmentation, wrinkles, and photoaging (premature ageing of the skin caused by repeated exposure to UV radiation). Ga-12 12%W/W Cream has antibacterial, antioxidant,  keratolytic (removes warts and calluses), comedolytic (inhibits the formation of blemishes), and anti-inflammatory activity.\nGa-12 12%W/W Cream contains ‘Glycolic acid’, which works by increasing the turnover rate of epithelial cells (cells that line the surface of the skin), eventually helping in peeling the skin and treating comedones (skin-coloured, small bumps due to acne).  Ga-12 12%W/W Cream kills bacteria, reduces inflammation, and unplugs blocked pores. It decomposes to release oxygen when applied to the skin. This oxygen acts as a bactericidal agent and kills Propionibacterium acnes, the bacteria that causes acne.\nGa-12 12%W/W Cream is for external use only. Avoid contact with eyes, eyelids, lips, mouth, and nose. If the medicine comes in contact with any of these areas, rinse with water immediately. Do not use Ga-12 12%W/W Cream on sunburned, windburned, dry, or irritated skin. Common side effects of Ga-12 12%W/W Cream include dry skin, erythema (skin redness), burning sensation, itching, skin irritation, and skin rash.\nGa-12 12%W/W Cream can make the skin more sensitive in the sunlight, hence always use sunscreen and protective clothing before you step outdoors. Care should be taken while applying Ga-12 12%W/W Cream on sensitive areas, such as the neck. Please limit the use of products that contain large amounts of alcohol (astringents, shaving creams, or after-shave lotions), hair removal products, and products containing lime or spices while using Ga-12 12%W/W Cream.\nGa-12 12%W/W Cream contains ‘Glycolic acid, an exfoliative agent used to treat skin problems like acne (pimples), acne scars, melasma, hyperpigmentation, photoaging, and seborrhea. It is an organic compound derived from sugarcane with an antibacterial, antioxidant,  keratolytic (removes warts and calluses), comedolytic (inhibits the formation of blemishes), and anti-inflammatory activity. Ga-12 12%W/W Cream increases the turnover rate of epithelial cells (cells that line the surface of the skin), eventually helps in peeling the skin and treats comedones (skin-coloured, small bumps due to acne).  Ga-12 12%W/W Cream kills bacteria, reduces inflammation, and unplugs blocked pores. It decomposes to release oxygen when applied to the skin. This oxygen acts as a bactericidal agent and kills Propionibacterium acnes, the bacteria that causes acne.', 423.00, NULL, 0, '[]', '[]', '[]', NULL, 0, 1, 1, '0', 0, 0, 0, 100, 'Tube', 0.00, 1, NULL, 302.00, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'flat_rate', 0.00, 0, NULL, 0, 'KLM Laboratories Glycolic Acid Cream 12% W/W GA - 12Price in BD', 'KLM Laboratories Glycolic Acid Cream 12% W/W GA - 12 Price in Bangladesh', NULL, NULL, 'klm-laboratories-glycolic-acid-cream-12-ww-ga-12', 0.00, 0, 0.00, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Buy Now', 0, '2026-02-11 13:41:25', '2026-02-11 13:41:25'),
